during the pandemic crisis the  communication sector took an essential  role  especially during the period of  isolation and confinement that was  imposed  to the portuguese population our  networks and our technology have enabled  us to ensure  that the portuguese population could  continue to work to perform  their normal duties that our youngsters  could continue to do  their learning through remote education  and that we could take  remote health to everybody this besides  keeping of course the businesses  up and running this was only possible  due to the large investments that altis  portugal has made in the last few years  throughout the country an investment  made in the optical fiber deployment  but also on the 4g expansion this  private investment has allowed portugal  not only to cope positively with this  confinement period  but also to have one of the highest  penetration rates of optical fiber  through the population  and we were able to do all this to cope  with the challenges and the growing  demands of traffic  that we've seen throughout the pandemic  crisis and the confinement  because we have reached over 5.3 million  households in optical fiber  in the country and also around 99.5  coverage of 4g networks in our country  so  i would say that technology the  communications and and the optical fire  networks  have been decisive in this pandemic  crisis and they will for sure  be decisive for the future  you
 

